.TH KINTSUGI-CONTEXT 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-context \- manage CONTEXT.md
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi context
init [\-\-force]
.br
.B kintsugi context
show
.br
.B kintsugi context
why "<question>"
.br
.B kintsugi context
diff
.br
.B kintsugi context
apply [\-\-all] [\-\-gated]
.br
.B kintsugi context
curate
.br
.B kintsugi context
refresh [\-\-apply]
.br
.B kintsugi context
attest
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage CONTEXT.md, the operator-authored document that defines authorization,
domain, and scope. It is injected on every turn.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP "\fBinit\fR"
Create CONTEXT.md. On a TTY an authorization template is picked from a menu;
\fB--template\fR takes the choice directly. Every template ships a worked
Authorization & scope example marked for replacement with the operator's own
words — the curator gate is untouched.

.IP \fBinit\fR
Create CONTEXT.md from template
.IP \fBshow\fR
Show sections, hashes, gated markers
.IP \fBwhy\fR
Which injected context line says this
.IP \fBdiff\fR
Review curator proposals
.IP \fBapply\fR
Apply auto-accepted proposals
.IP \fBcurate\fR
Run the curator over a session
.IP \fBrefresh\fR
Rebuild Current state from signals
.IP \fBattest\fR
Record operator review of Authorization & scope
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing file (init)
.IP \fB\-\-all\fR
Apply every non-gated proposal
.IP \fB\-\-gated\fR
Include authorization/scope proposals
.IP \fB\-\-apply\fR
Write changes (refresh)
.SH EXAMPLES
Initialize CONTEXT.md:
.PP
  $ kintsugi context init
.PP
Show context structure:
.PP
  $ kintsugi context show
.PP
Find context for a question:
.PP
  $ kintsugi context why "what databases can I access?"
.PP
Review curator proposals:
.PP
  $ kintsugi context diff
.PP
Apply proposals:
.PP
  $ kintsugi context apply --all
.PP
Attest authorization:
.PP
  $ kintsugi context attest
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1)
